<!-- Listen-friendly content -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: InteractiveAvatar</h2>
    <p>InteractiveAvatar is a real-time streaming avatar generation framework that addresses two fundamental problems. First, temporal drift: when streaming avatar methods generate video chunk by chunk with only a small look-back window, the avatar's visual appearance gradually diverges from the reference over long durations. Second, shallow interaction: audio-driven methods can lip-sync to speech but cannot understand user intent to perform specific physical actions.</p>
    <p>The paper introduces two mechanisms. Long-Short Visual Memory maintains a dual-buffer system: a FIFO short-term queue of recent frames for local continuity, and a fixed-capacity long-term buffer of semantically diverse keyframes for global consistency. Dynamic Key-Frame Selection uses SigLIP2 semantic features and a cosine similarity redundancy score to decide which frames earn a permanent long-term slot — only frames that reduce global redundancy are accepted. The Reasoning-Reaction Module routes user speech through an LLM that produces an action prompt, audio response, and stable-state prompt simultaneously. State-Cycling alternates between an action phase and a stable phase to prevent motion drift. Cache-Switching surgically refreshes KV cache entries when the prompt changes to reduce latency.</p>
    <p>On 500 test videos, InteractiveAvatar achieves the highest object consistency score of 85.2, the best text-video alignment of 25.93, and runs at 26.68 frames per second — the only method exceeding the real-time threshold of 24 FPS. Removing the LSVM drops object consistency by 6.8 points; removing the DMD distillation collapses frame rate from 26.68 to 1.27 — a 21-fold slowdown.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：InteractiveAvatar</h2>
    <p>InteractiveAvatar 是一个实时流式虚拟形象生成框架，解决了两个核心问题。其一是时间漂移：流式生成方法逐块生成视频时，仅能回顾最近几个块，导致生成时长增加后虚拟形象的外观逐渐偏离参考图像。其二是浅层交互：音频驱动的方法只能做口型同步，无法理解用户意图并执行具体的肢体动作。</p>
    <p>论文提出两个机制。长短视觉记忆（LSVM）维护双缓冲系统：一个近期帧的 FIFO 短期队列保证局部连续性，一个语义多样性高的关键帧固定容量长期缓冲区保证全局一致性。动态关键帧选择（DKFS）利用 SigLIP2 语义特征和余弦相似度冗余分数，决定哪些帧可以进入长期缓冲区——只有能降低全局冗余度的帧才被接受。推理-反应模块（RRM）将用户语音通过 ASR 转文字后输入大语言模型，同时产生动作指令、语音回复和稳定态提示词。状态循环策略在动作阶段与稳定阶段之间切换，防止动作漂移。缓存切换机制在提示词更新时精准刷新 KV 缓存，降低响应延迟。</p>
    <p>在 500 个测试视频上，InteractiveAvatar 的物体一致性得分 85.2 排名第一，文本-视频对齐 25.93 同样最优，生成速度达 26.68 帧每秒，是唯一超过 24 FPS 实时门槛的方法。去除 LSVM 导致物体一致性下降 6.8 个百分点；去除 DMD 蒸馏则使帧率从 26.68 骤降至 1.27，减慢 21 倍。</p>
  </div>
</div>

